/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The elastic element is the metal part that carries the load.
   - Four active gauges form a full bridge, placed so that two arms rise and two fall.
   - Vo is bridge output in V; Vs is excitation in V; GF is the gauge factor; ε is the axial strain; ν is Poisson’s ratio (about 0.3 for steel).
   - A load cell is sold by its ratings.
   - Mechanical stops limit travel under overload, and hermetic sealing keeps moisture out of the gauge area.
   - Torque is a twisting moment.
   - T is torque in N·m; F is force in N; r is radius in m.
   - P is shaft power in W; N is speed in rev/min; T is torque in N·m.
   - A full bridge on the shaft uses four gauges at ±45°.
   - A stationary frame can measure reaction torque: mount the motor or pump on bearings and measure the restraining force at a known radius.
*/
