/* book exam traps: Using the quarter-bridge formula for a four-active-gauge load cell. That under-reads by a factor of four. | Confusing rated capacity with safe overload and ultimate overload. Rated capacity is the specified working load; safe overload is an occasional higher load; ultimate overload may damage the cell. | Bonding torque gauges along the shaft axis. Torsion gives principal strains at 45° to the axis, so axial gauges see little useful strain. | Reading sensitivity as output volts instead of millivolts per volt of excitation. A 2 mV/V cell at 5 V gives only 10 mV at full load. | Using Vs·GF·ε for a column cell. Its transverse gauges see only νε, so the output is Vs·GF·ε(1 + ν)/2, about 65 % as much. */
