/* book exam traps: Putting Celsius into the β equation. It needs absolute temperature; add 273.15 to both T and T₀ before you divide. | Quoting R₀ at the wrong temperature. For an RTD, R₀ is at 0 °C; for a thermistor, the quoted value is usually at 25 °C. | Forgetting the leads. In a two-wire Pt100 circuit 0.385 Ω of lead resistance is a full 1 °C of error, and the error drifts with cable temperature. | Ignoring self-heating. The element sits above the surroundings by I²RT / PD, and that error grows in still air where PD is small. */
